{"id": "EUVD-2026-66495", "enisaUuid": "e13ae6f2-0258-38ae-8694-09bb663b8576", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nfbdev: bound mode sysfs output to the sysfs buffer\n\nmode_string() uses snprintf() which can return a value larger than the\nremaining buffer space. show_modes() accumulates the return value into i\nwithout checking whether i has reached PAGE_SIZE, causing the offset to\nadvance past the sysfs buffer if the modelist is long enough.\n\nAdd a size parameter to mode_string() and use scnprintf() to return\nonly the bytes actually written. Add an early return when offset\nalready exceeds the buffer. In show_modes(), stop accumulating once\nthe buffer is full.", "datePublished": "2026-08-26T14:37:37", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-16T19:26:28", "baseScore": 7.8, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/873a1aa15c313263f2e18b38cf525623cc4fabf6", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/d15d51fb26e830af58f3f21964f1c09c239077ea"], "aliases": ["GHSA-28cj-v8rj-mq63", "CVE-2026-80580"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.11, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "19b4f782-1840-3389-a890-5c65918c9096", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "34def7ff-c212-34b3-9467-7886df75ec1c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.1.10"}, {"id": "7004420c-1ce2-3390-b84b-e4bc64c19507", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2"}, {"id": "79c4d4f0-8519-393e-b7c9-96b025663761", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "2.6.12"}, {"id": "a3075546-e0f8-361b-a53d-1a3d239bdc27", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "1da177e4c3f41524e886b7f1b8a0c1fc7321cac2 <873a1aa15c313263f2e18b38cf525623cc4fabf6"}, {"id": "a4857afb-676d-3b35-8d6a-3e6